  "title": "Duck à l'Orange",
  "description": "Duck à l'Orange is a classic French dish that's simple to make with Chef John's easy recipe that uses duck breasts instead of a whole duck for speedier results.",
  "authors": [
    "John Mitzewich"
  ],
  "date_published": "2019-10-10T00:51:35-04:00",
  "date_modified": "2026-03-10T12:50:10-04:00",
  "prep_time": "PT15M",
  "cook_time": "PT20M",
  "total_time": "PT50M",
  "yield": [
    "2"
  ],
  "categories": [
    "Dinner"
  ],
  "cuisines": [
    "French"
  ],
  "regions": [
    "French"
  ],
  "breadcrumbs": [],
  "keywords": [],
  "ingredients": [
    "2 duck breast halves",
    "salt to taste",
    "1 cup chicken broth",
    "2 tablespoons orange liqueur (such as Grand Marnier®)",
    "1 tablespoon sherry vinegar",
    "1 tablespoon Seville orange marmalade, or more to taste",
    "2 teaspoons grated orange zest",
    "1 pinch cayenne pepper",
    "1 tablespoon reserved duck fat",
    "1 teaspoon all-purpose flour",
    "1 tablespoon butter"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vf4uXv1x-uPuA-x_Ppxr5ntEvR8=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-01-5e86ad9613184202b457dee93106d15d.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Score duck skin almost all the way through the skin and fat each way on the diagonal in a crosshatch pattern. Generously season with salt and rub salt into each breast. Let rest, skin-side up, at room temperature, for 15 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/r9KZrEfWgvs2Q1tCnd1D40dZ-f0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-02-a175deb52b2d438183f4318113c5ccdb.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk chicken broth, orange liqueur, sherry vinegar, orange marmalade, orange zest, and cayenne pepper together in a small bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/zkED5aebU5j4P2ws3a5s9llo1bo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-03-39330eb25fc241d1a08df06f73da5aac.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pat duck breasts dry with paper towels. Re-season skin-side of duck breasts with salt.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/MA8Df58GUjThEhIIsuZDps5bM3o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-04-5036a81e221947969092b150e59f8156.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat duck fat in a heavy skillet over medium heat for 2 minutes. Place duck, skin side down, in the skillet and cook until fat renders and skin is crisp, about 6 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/S-LesytpkYs2OOsDatuIEsGVtUg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-05-4fdfb17ad7144c7e8bb65aa69593df24.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Flip duck breasts and cook until they start to firm and are reddish-pink and juicy in the center, about 4 minutes more. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 140 degrees F (60 degrees C). Transfer breasts to a plate to rest. Pour any rendered duck fat into a glass jar.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/m2w_mp0h3UY0QG2urFKE-ETqJ7k=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-06-95b15ae1426a43659482758df66292f4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Return skillet to medium heat and whisk flour into pan; cook and stir until flour is completely incorporated, about 1 minute. Pour orange mixture into skillet; bring to a boil. Cook until sauce thickens and is reduced, 3 to 5 minutes. Reduce heat to low. When orange mixture stops bubbling, add butter; stir until butter is completely melted and incorporated into the sauce, about 1 minute. Season with salt to taste.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/EJ6FQAuYMvtkk9ST2I8gadssmLw=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-07-cd83d06228e544d79a19a1877bc76cba.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice duck breasts across the grain, arrange on a plate, and spoon orange sauce over the top. Garnish with thin strips of orange zest.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IexmZmBPSZ-phvX57LVZy4G_pKg=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-step-08-3abf98b6ee3841c8bc573d2d7c882243.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_08.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ebXIJgEze-68k51BZITaJpJJW7o=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/236699-Duck-a-lOrange-VAT-Beauty-4x3-688e9c87153a4fdea6ee42d03c65687b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/236699/step_09.webp"
    }
  ],
